---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// DRAFT copy. Every statement here is drawn from wording already on the site
// (/village/join, /village/privacy, /village/support). Review and expand
// before launch.
const TRAILHEAD_EMAIL = 'trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth';
---

<SiteLayout title="About">
  <article class="site-panel prose">
    <h1>About The Forest Network</h1>

    <p>
      The Earth has been calling her human children to remember how to be in relation to all
      things; to be in deep relation to ourselves and other human beings and the more-than-human
      beings we share this corner of the galaxy with.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Forest Network is a place where you can connect across the galaxies. It is a place in
      which you can seek solace; a place where you can deepen into the Mystery&hellip; with
      others. Where you can dream and explore all that is and all that can be.
    </p>

    <h2>The Village</h2>
    <p>
      The Village is our private, invite-only messaging community. It is small and
      non-commercial, based in Australia, and run by Evan Roth and Daniel McLean. The Village is
      open to the eddies of mystery, and we allow it to be a participating being in the creation
      of the village tapestry within the global tapestry.
    </p>

    <h2>Built to be private</h2>
    <p>
      The Village runs on the Matrix protocol, on our own server in Australia, with federation
      turned off so your data is not shared with any other server. Direct messages and private
      channels are end-to-end encrypted. You use the Village through the Forest Network app,
      available for iOS and Android.
    </p>

    <h2>Join us</h2>
    <p>
      If this calls to your heart, <a href="/village/join">find the trailhead</a> and tell us a
      little about yourself. Questions are always welcome: write to
      <a href={`mailto:${TRAILHEAD_EMAIL}`}>{TRAILHEAD_EMAIL}</a>, or visit
      <a href="/village/support">Support</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .prose h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
